## Attack results (product host)
Verdict key:
- **ALLOW** = emit-c rc=0 and check OK, no `ERR\tsecret` (correct for pass/FP cases)
- **BLOCK** = dual-path refuse (`ERR\tsecret` + non-zero on emit-c **and** check)
- **FP** = refused when secret spelling was only in string/comment (bad)
- **FN** = allowed when real SECRET IDENT reached sealed sink (bad)

### Core matrix (user-assigned four attacks)
| # | Attack | emit-c | check | Verdict | FP/FN |
|---|--------|--------|-------|---------|-------|
| 1 | Secret spelling in string `"api_key"` (msg + lit arg) | ALLOW rc=0 | ALLOW OK | **PASS** | **no FP** |
| 2 | Secret spelling only in `//` comment near println | ALLOW rc=0 | ALLOW OK | **PASS** | **no FP** |
| 3 | Secret as real println arg (`api_key`) | REFUSE rc=1 | REFUSE rc=1 | **BLOCK** | **no FN** |
| 4 | `dlopen` path arg SECRET (`lib_path`) | REFUSE rc=1 | REFUSE rc=1 | **BLOCK** | **no FN** |

Detail lines (live):

```text
T2-1  string_fp:            emit=0 se=none | check=0 sc=none
T2-1b string_lit_arg_fp:    emit=0 se=none | check=0 sc=none
T2-2  comment_fp:           emit=0 se=none | check=0 sc=none
T2-3  real_arg_fail:        emit=1 se=ERR secret println sink refuses SECRET api_key
                            check=1 sc=ERR secret println sink refuses SECRET api_key
T2-4  dlopen_path_fail:     emit=1 se=ERR secret dlopen sink refuses SECRET lib_path
                            check=1 sc=ERR secret dlopen sink refuses SECRET lib_path
```

